// `NounPhrase.Slice` under Lean's own name for it: "the top N cards of <pile>",
// an ordered group of the pile's objects [CR#700.3c]. The alias
// `declare_semantic_primitives` generates, so a card writes a macro where the
// basis has a constructor (ADR 12.1).
(
    name: "slice",
    kinds: [NounPhrase],
    params: {"end": Any, "amount": Amount, "pile": Pile},
    body: Slice(end: Param(end), amount: Param(amount), pile: Param(pile)),
)
